# A test of the owner's idea (2026-10-05): the line keeps its fire until the skirmishers behind it have
# fired, then gives its volley into an enemy already shaken and blinded by smoke. Put Skirmishers (or
# any shooters) in the rank behind; on its own it behaves like Line that waits until 35 paces.
drill "Patient Line"
about "Line that holds its fire until the rank behind it has fired (or the enemy is within 35), then volleys. Meant to stand in front of Skirmishers."
type Even
dials aggression 0.50 discipline 0.85 cohesion 0.90 cover 0.20 patience 0.70 nerve 0.75

sergeant:
  when enemy charging and enemy within 40              -> hold; stand fast; volley at 30
  when losing the exchange                             -> fall back 30
  when winning the exchange                            -> press; form tight
  when rank behind firing and enemy within 60          -> hold; form tight; fire at will
  when enemy within 35                                 -> hold; form tight; fire at will
  when enemy within 60                                 -> hold; form tight; hold fire
  otherwise                                            -> advance; form tight

man:
  when alone                                           -> keep slot tight
  when enemy within 6                                  -> bayonet
  when enemy charging and loaded and enemy within 40   -> fire
  when enemy charging                                  -> keep slot tight
  when rank behind firing and loaded and enemy within 60 -> fire
  when loaded and enemy within 35                      -> fire
  otherwise                                            -> follow sergeant
